.TH MMTREADER 1 "August 2026" "MMT-Reader 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mmtReader \- deep packet inspection and per-protocol network statistics tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mmtReader
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mmtReader
analyzes network traffic from pcap capture files or live network interfaces and produces
per-protocol statistics including packet counts, data volume, payload volume, and protocol
path hierarchies. It leverages the MMT-DPI library for deep packet inspection and protocol
classification.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-trace <file>
Analyze a pcap capture file (offline mode). No root privileges required.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interface <iface>
Capture traffic from a live network interface (online mode). Requires root privileges.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-buffer <MB>
Set the pcap handler buffer size in megabytes for live capture (default: 50).
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-paths
Show per-protocol-path statistics (e.g., TCP.HTTP.Google).
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress progress output. Only final results are shown.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Show verbose debug output to stderr (does not affect stdout output).
.TP
.B \-C, \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI color output.
.TP
.B \-x <0|1>
Enable (1) or disable (0) IP address-based classification (default: 1).
.TP
.B \-y <0|1>
Enable (1) or disable (0) hostname-based classification (default: 1).
.TP
.B \-z <0|1>
Enable (1) or disable (0) port-based classification (default: 1).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B MMTREADER_JSON
Set to B1R to force JSON output mode.
.TP
.B MMTREADER_NO_COLOR
Set to B1R to disable color output (same as \fB\-\-no-color\fR).
.TP
.B MMTREADER_QUIET
Set to B1\fR to enable quiet mode (same as \fB\-\-quiet\fR).
.br
Command-line flags override environment variables.
.SH EXAMPLES
Analyze a pcap file with protocol paths:
.IP
.B mmtReader \-t capture.pcap \-a
.TP
Live capture on eth0 with a 100 MB buffer:
.IP
.B sudo mmtReader \-i eth0 \-b 100 \-a
.TP
Disable IP classification:
.IP
.B mmtReader \-t capture.pcap \-a \-x 0
.TP
MMP-only mode (disable all classification):
.IP
.B mmtReader \-t capture.pcap \-a \-x 0 \-y 0 \-z 0
.SH OUTPUT
At the end of execution, mmtReader prints:
.RS
.IP \(bu 3
Protocol statistics with path (if \fB\-a\fR is set)
.IP \(bu 3
Protocol statistics (aggregated)
.IP \(bu 3
Input statistics summary (packets, volume, sessions, duration, bandwidth)
.IP \(bu 3
PCAP statistics (online mode only: received packets and kernel drops)
.RE
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Requires the MMT-DPI library installed at \fB/opt/mmt/dpi/\fR.
Install from: https://bitbucket.org/montimage/mmt-dpi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful analysis or \fB\-\-help\fR requested.
.TP
.B 1
Help was printed (legacy).
.TP
.B 2
Usage or validation error.
